<example><exercise>
  <problem> 
    <para>Select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>Completing the square method:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl} 4 x^{2}-28 x+29 &amp;=&amp;0 \\
    \frac{4 x^{2}-28 x+29}{4} &amp;=&amp;0 \\
    x^{2}-7 x+\frac{29}{4} &amp;=&amp;0 \\
    x^{2}-7 x &amp;=&amp;-\frac{29}{4} \\
    x^{2}-7 x+\left(\frac{7}{2}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp;-\frac{29}{4}+\left(\frac{7}{2}\right)^{2} \\
    x^{2}-7 x+\frac{49}{4} &amp;=&amp;\frac{20}{4} \\
    x^{2}-7 x+\frac{49}{4} &amp;=&amp;5 \\
    \left(x-\frac{7}{2}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp;5 \\ \sqrt{\left(x-\frac{7}{2}\right)^{2}} &amp;=&amp;\sqrt{5} \\
    x-\frac{7}{2} &amp;=&amp;\pm \sqrt{5} \\ x&amp;=&amp;\frac{7}{2}\pm\sqrt{5} \\ x&amp;=&amp;\frac{7}{2}+\sqrt{5} \\ x&amp;=&amp;\frac{7}{2}-\sqrt{5} \\
    x&amp;=&amp;\frac{7}{2}+\sqrt{5} \text { and } x=\frac{7}{2}-\sqrt{5}
    \end{array}
    \) </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
